 let mut md=String::from("# Joint narrow-top G2 digit reduction: work screen\n\nA new native prototype is selected for qualification: group points by the two existing signed six-bit top digits, then coalesce both reduction stages. On the two saved real inputs, this removes **20.6% / 20.2% of generic top-window additions**, and reduces modeled tree-layer calls **3,289→226 / 3,345→227**. These are algebra/topology counts, not measured speedups. Production and accepted proof latency stay unchanged.\n\n## Algorithm\n\nWithin each existing G2 point-range half, group original points by their top digit pair(a,b), excluding(0,0). Reduce each occupied pair class once. Its derived sum then contributes to both original component marginals, with the original signs, phi map and bucket weights. The ten lower windows, Phi2 decomposition, 12-bit reader and two parts stay unchanged. No all-row-pair search, scalar recoding, shifted key, persistent point table or new field arithmetic is used.\n\nThe first tree groups256 adjacent compact pair classes through the existing group_affine algorithm. The selected second stage uses that same algorithm across each128-sign-bin marginal. This changes parallelism as well as work. A larger marginal leaf can reduce available parallelism, increase scratch and lose in practice; native timing is required. No generic frontend counter capture was repeated: retained IBS/dispatch studies already favor investigating arithmetic/resource costs over a frontend-only explanation. [Scope/history audit](source/history-audit.md).\n\n## Both declared results\n\nThe first layout coalesced only joint classes and retained original per-bin indexed marginals. It **fails** its necessary gate: primary tree layers rise3,289→3,301, despite fewer additions. A separate follow-up coalesces the marginals too; it uses the same count-gate conditions and **passes**. The old helper, protocol, observations and failed gate remain intact. No threshold changes, favorable subset, capture rerun or performance adoption occurs.\n\n| Shape | Original top additions | Both layouts: additions after | Saved | First layout: tree layers | Follow-up: tree layers | Original / follow-up scalar tail pairs |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
