 md.push_str("\nPrimary saves11,298 generic additions;2×2 saves11,478. The exact identity is saved = input rows with both digits nonzero − occupied classes with both digits nonzero, applied separately to both halves. The separate first layout's scalar tails also fall, but its primary layer-count condition fails. Coalesced-independent counts without joint sharing are retained as attribution only; they do not remove additions or qualify a runtime alternative.\n\nThe necessary gate requires exact algebra/source/fixture checks, strictly fewer generic additions and no increase in tree-layer calls on both real shapes. It has no minimum percentage threshold. Tree calls are not measured inversions; prefix selection, scalar tails and lane groups are modeled from nonexceptional pairs, with the existing32-pair threshold. Actual identities/cancellations/doublings, queue behavior, task cost, caches, inversion service and wall time remain unmodeled. Sign/component/part merges and final weighting are common and omitted from the addition totals. No conversion to removable proof time is justified.\n\n## Correctness and provenance\n\nThe exact existing fixtures and their independent complete-MSM oracle receipts are reused. No old oracle repeats. Accepted stable zero-aware grouping declines primary(30,089 rows) and admits2×2(52,274→28,852). Grouped intermediate curve cancellation is unknown; the structural model assumes nonexceptional points. The current accepted source manifest, reused library source recovery, exact copied grouping/Phi/Booth functions, canonical scalar/point encoding and on-curve inputs are checked.\n\nFour original model tests pass once, followed by two new follow-up tests. The latter invocation filters out the four already successful tests. Cases cover empty/odd/skewed/dense signed pair populations, zero pairs/digits, identities, signed64 extrema,256-class group and1024-point tile boundaries, structural occupancy, exact tree-edge counts and lane/tail accounting. Both real populations reconstruct Phi/Booth scalars and run two independent full-width Fr-token streams per layout, checking every signed marginal bin and the weighted top sum. These symbolic/field-token checks do not qualify a new real-curve kernel. Unchanged production suites are inherited, not rerun.\n\nBoth four-step source-pinned Rust xtask workflows complete on first executions:425 original pins,433 follow-up pins. Every command exit and stdout/stderr hash is checked. No native helper, test or successful count reruns. The follow-up inherits original baseline counts by exact saved-row identity. Its addition totals and occupied pair classes agree with the original layout; only reduction topology changes. The original top addition counts54,829/56,687 also match the earlier balanced-window census.\n\n## Memory limits of this screen\n\nA129×129 histogram admits at most16,640 nonzero digit-pair classes. Compact u16 labels avoid allocating a full point grid. Original key points are borrowed; shared sums are derived proof-local points. Native routing can reuse the histogram as scatter cursors, then drop it; original order/starts/counts can drop after joint sums. That lifetime design is not implemented or qualified.\n\n| Shape / half | Occupied classes U | Routing payload KiB | First reduction held KiB | Follow-up marginal retained KiB |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
 for(a,b)in old.iter().zip(&new){for(x,y)in a["parts"].as_array().unwrap().iter().zip(b["parts"].as_array().unwrap()){writeln!(md,"| {} / {} | {} | {:.2} | {:.2} | {:.2} |",a["shape"].as_str().unwrap(),x["part"],x["occupied_pair_classes"],x["routing_requested_payload_bytes"].as_f64().unwrap()/1024.,x["first_reduction_held_payload_bytes"].as_f64().unwrap()/1024.,y["coalesced_marginal_retained_payload_before_leaf_bytes"].as_f64().unwrap()/1024.).unwrap();}}
